games:
  -
    title: "Fae's Anatomy"
    category: "megagames"
    banner: "images/faes-banner.avif"
    status: "for_sale"
    summary: |
      In the near future magic has returned and everything seems peaceful in the land of Swanshire.

      A megagame of magic medicine and mischief.
    description: |
      Designed by John Keyworth, Patrick Rose and Holly Wall

      In the not too distant future, magic returns to the British Isles. Fæ emerge from under their hills and the world is forever changed.

      The demesne of Swanshire is a peaceful collection of communes on the coast. It has a thriving magically-active community and two world class hospitals… Swan’s Cliff and Wellspring Hospitals.

      Hospital Researchers have recently been complaining of a strange dissonance flowing through the local ley lines. It’s probably nothing.

      Previously ran through <a href="https://www.penninemegagames.co.uk/faes-anatomy.html">Pennine Megagames (2022)</a>, <a href="https://www.readingmegagames.com/fae-s-anatomy">Reading Megagames (2023)</a>, <a href="https://www.melbournemegagames.com/fae-s-anatomy">Melbourne Megagames (2023)</a> and <a href="https://www.facebook.com/events/1081144963121089/?active_tab=discussion">Adelaide Megagames (2024)</a>.

      **The game is available to purchase on ich.io.**
    link: "https://drugcrazed.itch.io/faes-anatomy"
    link_type: "purchase"
  -
    title: "The Raven Banner"
    category: "megagames"
    status: "for_sale"
    banner: "images/ravenbanner-banner.avif"
    summary: |
      A small megagame set during the 870s about the viking invasion of England and the establishment of Danelaw.
    description: |
      For decades Danish raiders have been pillaging the coasts of England, but recently the “Great Heathen Army” conquered the northernmost kingdom of Northumbria.

      As a Saxon aristocrat or Danish raider you will be fighting and negotiating to ensure the best future for yourselves in this chaotic and violent era.

      The Raven Banner is a megagame, although smaller and shorter than most. Players will be asked to use the game’s rules and negotiate with the other players in order to achieve goals provided to them on their unique player briefings. The overall aim of the game is to explore a historically plausible version of the 9th century Viking invasion of England.

      A game of The Raven Banner lasts approximately 3 hours and there are 12 to 16 players, plus 2 organisers who keep the game running smoothly.

      This game pack will give you everything you need to print out at home to play the game - facilitators and players guide, player sheets, maps and cards. It also contains files suitable for sending to professional printers for a nicer looking copy. You will also need 4 decks of cards and 16 six sided dice.
    options:
      -
        description: "The players guide is available to download for free."
        link: "https://www.kiwigamedesign.co.uk/_files/ugd/9e54e1_a18e09953c1644b5a9561cd712bb7765.pdf"
        type: "download"
      -
        description: "The full game pack, fulfilled through DriveThruRPG, for £15."
        link: "https://www.paypal.com/cgi-bin/webscr?cmd=_xclick&business=jkeywo%40yahoo%2eco%2euk&lc=GB&item_name=The%20%Raven%20%Banner&amount=15%2e00&currency_code=GBP&button_subtype=services&bn=PP%2dBuyNowBF%3abtn_buynowCC_LG%2egif%3aNonHosted"
        type: "purchase"
  -
    title: "Den of Wolves: New Eden"
    category: "megagames"
    status: "for_sale"
    banner: "images/neweden-banner.avif"
    summary: |
      A small megagame where players lead a space fleet of survivors fleeing a massive attack.
    description: |
      In this game you will play a member of a space fleet, survivors of a massive attack from the nation of Wolf - decimating and subjugating the other settled worlds. Together you will be trying to survive in space, flee further Wolf attacks and find a new home for your people - a New Eden.

      The game runs for 8 to 18 players over 3 to 4 hours, split into 8 turns. The game plays in real time, so managing your time and delegating tasks is an important part of the game.

      Each player will be assigned a role of one of the survivor fleet space ships and must work together to succeed. Each ship represents a team of players and each come from a different nation or colony from before the attack.

      Beware, however, Wolf planted agents throughout the colonies before the attack and it’s highly probable that some will be hiding amongst other players in the fleet.

      **December 2025 Update** - The game has been expanded with an optional 7th ship - the SANS Capybara - taking the player count up to 20.
    options:
      -
        description: "The players guide is available to download for free."
        link: "https://www.kiwigamedesign.co.uk/_files/ugd/9e54e1_56c3cba05bee40f2b3cbb2a1da7e8351.pdf"
        type: "download"
      -
        description: "The full game pack, fulfilled through DriveThruRPG, for £30."
        link: "https://www.paypal.com/cgi-bin/webscr?cmd=_xclick&business=jkeywo%40yahoo%2eco%2euk&lc=GB&item_name=Den%20%of%20%Wolves:%20%New%20%Eden&amount=30%2e00&currency_code=GBP&button_subtype=services&bn=PP%2dBuyNowBF%3abtn_buynowCC_LG%2egif%3aNonHosted"
        type: "purchase"
  -
    title: "Crisis: Mars"
    category: "megagames"
    status: "for_sale"
    banner: "images/crisismars-banner.avif"
    summary: |
      A small megagame centred around a Mars colony fighting to war for independance from Earth.
    description: |
      Crisis: Mars is a small 2 1/2 hour megagame for up to 18 players, played in small teams with an emphasis on negotiation and simple rules.

      The year is 2241 and humanity has colonised the inner solar system with space stations and mining in the asteroid belt, and a colony and terraforming project on Mars. In recent years a growing movement on Mars is pushing for independence from the Unified Nations of Earth and they have just gained a majority in the Martian senate. You will take the role of an actor on the edge of this brewing conflict. You will have limited opportunity to change its course but conflict gives you the chance to achieve your own goals.
    options:
      -
        description: "The players guide is available to download for free."
        link: "https://www.kiwigamedesign.co.uk/_files/ugd/9e54e1_f680109ba26c4b258d63ac544d4b9656.pdf"
        type: "download"
      -
        description: "The full game pack, fulfilled through DriveThruRPG, for £15."
        link: "https://www.paypal.com/cgi-bin/webscr?cmd=_xclick&business=jkeywo%40yahoo%2eco%2euk&lc=GB&item_name=Crisis%20%Mars&amount=15%2e00&currency_code=GBP&button_subtype=services&bn=PP%2dBuyNowBF%3abtn_buynowCC_LG%2egif%3aNonHosted"
        type: "purchase"
  -
    title: "Crisis: Black Swan"
    category: "megagames"
    status: "in_development"
    summary: |
      A small megagame centred around geopolitics, global disasters and the inexplicable.
    description: |
      *Black Swan [blæk swɒn]: an event that is impossible to predict and has a dramatic impact.*

      International relief efforts, civil wars, political tormoil - the world is in crisis and you will take on the role of a national or global leader trying to navigate it.

      ...and then something inexplicaable happens to make things worse.

      Can you work out what's going on, and make the right decisions? And can you push your own agenda forward at the same time?

      Crisis: Black Swan is a narrative focused game of geopolitics meeting the unknown. Deploy your limited resources wisely and creatively, cooperate or betray, and create a shared narrative that shapes the world's future.
