  -
    title: "RPG Poems"
    category: "roleplaying"
    status: "free"
    banner: "images/rppoems-banner.avif"
    summary: "Roleplaying Poems are short, focused games that typically take less than 30 minutes to play."
    description: |
      Roleplaying Poems are short, focused games that typically take less than 30 minutes to play.
    options:
          -
            title: "The Life and Death of..."
            description: |
              A game to be played with a group of at least 3 friends while out for a walk. You will need something to use as a token you can easily pass around.
            
              Players use places and things they see on their walk as inspiration to describe an incident in someone's life,someone who you will follow from birth to death. Their life is touched by the peculiar.
            link: "https://www.kiwigamedesign.co.uk/_files/ugd/9e54e1_ad369135ef7946dd966833f139872b7f.pdf"
            type: "download"
          -
            title: "Artefact"
            description: |
              A quick 5 minute game for exactly 3 players it requires some kind of timekeeping device to play.

              Written out of nostalgia for the double edged magical artefacts of Advanced Dungeons and Dragons players explore the consiquences of using dangerous items to solve problems.
            link: "https://www.kiwigamedesign.co.uk/_files/ugd/9e54e1_e0d5ffa77854444ebb045aacb166c407.pdf"
            type: "download"
          -
            title: "Devils"
            description: |
              A game for 3 or more players (ideally 3-4) that takes about 20 minutes to play and requires a sheet of paper (or index card) and pen each.
              
              Devils follows the story of several people with problems who ask for devil for help, and the ill fated results.

              Inspired by <a href="https://appleofmyeye.bandcamp.com/track/devils">this song</a>.

            link: "https://www.kiwigamedesign.co.uk/_files/ugd/9e54e1_aafb9ba598724d9197c5c9edc7409d4d.pdf"
            type: "download"
          -
            title: "Ghosts of the Drowned"
            description: |
              A game for 4 or more players that takes 20 minutes to play.

              You play the titular Ghosts of the Drowned as they gather and tell tales of their death.

              Inspired by <a href="https://appleofmyeye.bandcamp.com/track/ghosts-of-the-drowned">this song</a>.
            link: "https://www.kiwigamedesign.co.uk/_files/ugd/9e54e1_1af74e10ff834606a50bf08c140b6f2f.pdf"
            type: "download"

  -
    title: "Annex"
    category: "roleplaying"
    status: "free"
    banner: "images/annex-banner.avif"
    summary: "Annex is a free roleplaying game based on the book Ancillary Justice and the mechanics are inspired by the Occupy movement’s hand signs."
    description: |
      Annex is a free roleplaying game that was play tested at London IndieMeet. The setting is based on the book Ancillary Justice and the mechanics are inspired by the Occupy movement’s hand signs.

      You don’t need to be familiar with the book, although reading at least the first two chapters will help (they are available as a free sample from Amazon, the one on Orbit’s website is only one chapter which isn’t enough to be helpful).
      
      Your group plays collectively as a single artificial intelligence that controls multiple Ancillary bodies. You, and at least 2 other players (preferably more), have been charged with bringing order to a recently conquered planet… spreading order and civilisation with military precision.

      The AI hive mind is simulated in play by using hand gestures that maintain consensus within the group. These are similar to those used by many activist groups (originally Occupy) for meetings and were easy to transfer into an RPG.

      After about 40 minutes of world building the game proceeds in a series of short stories, each around 40 minutes long until you want to stop. I takes at least 3 players but works better with more.
    link: "https://www.kiwigamedesign.co.uk/_files/ugd/9e54e1_aaca2a5fa1574bc9af0fd166aea356a2.pdf"
    link_type: "download"

  -
    title: "Intrepid Histories"
    category: "roleplaying"
    status: "on_hold"
    banner: "images/ih-banner.avif"
    summary: |
      Explore a historic journey, but set in an alternative history.

      Each scenario always follows the same journey, but the alternate history will be unique to your group.
    description: |
      Intrepid Histories is a storytelling game for 3-5 players that takes 2 to 2 1/2 hours to play.

      Explore a historic journey, but set in an alternative history.

      * Follow Napoleon's Grande Armee in the 1812 invasion of Russia.
      * Explore with Ferdinand Magellan on his circumnavigation of the globe.
      * March across the alps with Hanibal and his war elephants.
      * Embark on the Hajj with Mansa Musa.
      * Look for the lost tribe of the Yuezhi with Zhang Qian.
      * Hunt the Ripper through the streets of London.

      Each scenario always follows the same journey, but the alternate history will be unique to your group. Everythig you need to know about the real historic events will be provided by the scenario.

      This game has finished development, but final graphic design work is on hold.
